#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0499 expect=noViolation domain=ADAE
#note "dataset ADAE. Columns STUDYID(Char), USUBJID(Char), AEDECOD(Char), APERIOD(Num). ONE row: `CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | HEADACHE | 1`. The mirror of scenario 1: the COMPANION APERIOD is declared and the CONDITION variable ASPER is not, so the first conjunct `var_exists('ASPER')` is FALSE and the rule stays silent. This is the DISCRIMINATING direction test - it is the scenario that fails if the two operands are ever swapped. The rule has no wildcard and no scope gate here, so it executes and evaluates FALSE."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
dataset ADAE
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col AEDECOD type=Char
col APERIOD type=Num
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | HEADACHE | 1
